SECURITY-REVIEW.md:3:**Status:** source review and test-first/fix evidence are recorded for the confirmed findings below. C-05–C-08 remain unconfirmed review candidates. The SDK migration still needs its final test/devnet/coverage pass; those results remain owned by the migration work.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:7:**Evidence status:** source and audit-report review, plus targeted TestVM PoCs for the arithmetic and wrapper cases. Red/fix commits are separate for confirmed code defects. The fee-on-transfer PoCs first failed with 100 shares against 90 received assets; the follow-up assertions characterize that documented unsupported-asset behavior. At the time of this revision, the final green C-04 target rerun, full library suite, devnet E2E suite, benches, fuzzing/property runs, coverage, and WASM checks are still pending or being run by the migration agents. No claim of full migration validation is made here.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:11:The requested review scope is the whole library: `contracts/src/**`, `contracts-proc/src/**`, `lib/crypto/src/**`, examples, benches, fuzz targets, docs, and the SDK devnet test setup replacing `lib/e2e` and `lib/e2e-proc`. I reviewed the audited production source, the SDK-related production diff, storage declarations changed by the migration, and the new TestVM fixture at source level. Example-by-example devnet activation, fuzz/property execution, the full E2E replay, and storage-layout tooling remain part of the migration agent's unfinished validation.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:26:- **v0.2.0:** H-01 limb shift overflow (resolved); M-01 `ct_rem` underflow (resolved); M-02 custom trait selectors not matched to implementations (acknowledged/open); L-01 custom Merkle hashing commutativity documentation (resolved); L-02 carry/borrow types (resolved); L-03 zero bit count (resolved); L-04 hex parsing overflow (resolved); L-05 wrapper decimals (resolved); L-06 ERC4626 mutability (resolved); L-07 duplicate selectors (marked resolved; residual hash-collision gap is C-06); L-08 generated trait components (resolved); L-09 big-integer comparison timing (marked resolved); N-01–N-07 and N-09 (reported resolved); N-08 misleading docs (partially resolved); N-10 test coverage (acknowledged/open). The Poseidon2 parameter checks are additional recommendations, not counted findings.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:38:- **`VestingWallet`** (`contracts/src/finance/vesting_wallet.rs`): vested amount is zero before start, monotone during vesting, and reaches total historical allocation at/after end; released amounts never exceed vested amounts or total allocation; release transfers only the newly releasable amount; native and ERC20 accounting remain independent. Full-precision intermediate arithmetic is covered by fixed finding C-03.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:62:- **Address, math, storage slots** (`utils/address.rs`, `utils/math/**`, `utils/storage_slot.rs`): address calls distinguish code/no-code behavior as documented; checked math reverts on true overflow and does not reject representable full-precision results; storage slots do not collide with ordinary contract storage or standard proxy slots.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:79:| C-01 | Low — fixed | **ERC2981 zero denominator by default.** Fresh storage read zero and caused royalty queries to divide by zero. | Not in prior audits. Red PoC and fix are separate (`3083e7f`, `12eea1b`); `_fee_denominator` now treats stored zero as the 10,000 default, preserving storage layout. Targeted ERC2981 tests passed. |
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:80:| C-02 | Low — fixed | **ERC2981 intermediate overflow.** Large `sale_price * numerator` overflowed before division despite a representable quotient. | Not in prior audits. Red PoC and fix are separate (`6aa2e38`, `4c9d952`); `mul_div(..., Floor)` now gives full-precision floor division. Targeted ERC2981 tests passed. |
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:81:| C-03 | Low, range-dependent — fixed | **Vesting intermediate overflow.** A maximum allocation with elapsed time 2 and duration 3 overflowed before division despite a representable quotient. | Not in prior audits. Red PoC and fix are separate (`531faf0`, `a91c169`); vesting uses full-precision floor `mul_div`. Targeted vesting PoC passed after the fix. |
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:84:| C-06 | Low — fixed | **Selector collision check was textual, not selector-based.** Distinct canonical signatures `burn(uint256)` and `collate_propagate_storage(bytes16)` both use selector `0x42966c68`, but the macro accepted them. | Related to v0.2 L-07, which addressed duplicate textual signatures but not distinct-signature collisions. The baseline red trybuild passed compilation unexpectedly; the SDK selector equality assertion confirmed the collision. `21f9866` adds const comparisons using `stylus_sdk::function_selector!`; the targeted compile-fail test passes. |
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:109:The TestVM proxy unit tests mock delegated implementation responses; they cannot demonstrate actual deployed code executing under `delegatecall`, proxy storage persistence, or logs emitted from the proxy address. Earlier Motsu tests did exercise composed mock contracts. The SDK devnet E2E suite must retain those proxy outcomes, especially implementation isolation, constructor initialization, revert propagation, and upgrade authorization. Several proxy tests failed in the reported TestVM run because of shared return-data behavior; those failures are not evidence that production code is broken, but they are an unresolved validation gap until repaired or covered by devnet tests.
SECURITY-REVIEW.md:113:The final migration result still needs all compile/clippy/fmt/WASM checks, every v0.3 E2E success and failure case on devnet, benches, fuzz/property/differential evidence, and the baseline-to-final coverage comparison. These are outside this source-only finding review and should be reported by the migration owner with exact command output.

